<article class="legal-page section">
  <div class="prose section-shell">
    <p class="draft-banner"><strong>Draft for organizational and legal review.</strong> This notice is not approved for publication and does not constitute legal advice.</p>
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p><strong>Draft last updated:</strong> July 24, 2026</p>
    <p>This draft explains how the Caribbean Health AI Congress (“CHAIC,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) may collect, use, and share personal information when you visit chaicpr.com, register for CHAIC, read CHAIC articles, contact us, or interact with related event services.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We may receive information you choose to provide, such as your name, email address, organization, professional role, accessibility request, sponsorship interest, or the contents of a message. Registration and payment information entered in Luma is collected by Luma under its own terms and privacy notice; CHAIC may receive attendee and transaction records needed to administer the event.</p>
    <p>When you use the website, technical information may be collected automatically, including IP address, device and browser information, approximate location, referring page, pages viewed, link interactions, and cookie or similar-technology identifiers.</p>

    <h2>Website analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>We use Google Tag Manager to manage measurement tags. Tags may include Google Analytics 4 and Google Ads. These services may use cookies or similar technologies to measure website use, campaign performance, and actions such as registration-link clicks. Google may process device and activity information under its own privacy terms. We do not create a browser-side “purchase” event; completed registrations are recorded by Luma.</p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Luma:</strong> official registration and checkout, including attendee and payment-related processing.</li>
      <li><strong>Soro:</strong> source hosting for approved article text and images that CHAIC publishes as static pages.</li>
      <li><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> if a WhatsApp contact link is offered, opening it sends you to a service operated by Meta. The message and account information you provide are processed by WhatsApp.</li>
      <li><strong>External links:</strong> venue maps, speaker profiles, sponsor sites, and other linked services have their own privacy practices.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We may use information to operate and secure the website; administer registration and event access; answer questions; provide requested accessibility support; manage sponsor, speaker, press, or partner relationships; understand website and campaign performance; comply with legal obligations; and protect the rights, safety, and integrity of attendees and the event.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and choices</h2>
    <p>Analytics and advertising tags may store or read cookies. The final notice should describe the production consent controls and region-specific choices actually implemented before publication. You can also use browser settings to limit cookies, though doing so may affect some measurement or checkout enhancements. Standard Luma links remain available without CHAIC JavaScript.</p>

    <h2>Sharing, transfers, and retention</h2>
    <p>We may share information with vendors that support hosting, analytics, communications, registration, event operations, and security; with professional advisers; or when required by law. These providers may process information outside Puerto Rico or your country of residence, including in the United States. Appropriate contractual or legal safeguards should be confirmed before this draft is approved.</p>
    <p>We retain information only as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described, including event administration, financial and tax records, dispute resolution, security, and legal compliance. The final policy should state approved retention periods for attendee, inquiry, analytics, and marketing records.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or objection to certain processing, and to withdraw consent where processing relies on consent. These rights may be subject to legal exceptions. The final notice should identify the verified process and response timelines for applicable requests.</p>

    <h2>Children and sensitive information</h2>
    <p>The website and congress are intended for professionals and adult learners and are not directed to children. Do not send patient information, medical records, protected health information, passwords, payment-card details, or other unnecessary sensitive information by email or a general contact link.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or privacy requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. Before approval, the organization should confirm the responsible legal entity, mailing address, privacy contact, and any required regulator information.</p>
